course: dictionary
lesson: 14841
title: Rafts: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Rafts is one of these words. A raft is a flat platform that floats on water, and rafts is the plural, so it means more than one raft. «The children built rafts from old barrels and planks.» The clue is built: you build things to use them, and a raft floats on water.
explain: «Rafts of» is a phrase that means lots of. «There were rafts of ducklings on the pond.» The words there were and ducklings tell you the picture is about many ducklings, so rafts of means lots of here. Check by swapping in lots of: does the sentence still make sense?
explain: Rafts can also be a verb, an action word. When someone rafts, they travel on a raft. «Every summer, Sam rafts across the lake with his cousins.» Sam is doing the action, so rafts means travels on a raft. Look at who or what is doing the action to find the right meaning.
fact: A raft is a flat floating platform, often made of wood, logs or rubber.
fact: «Rafts» is the plural of raft, so it means more than one raft.
fact: «Rafts of» means lots of, as in «rafts of people» on a crowded beach.
fact: «He rafts» means he travels on a raft.
fact: Life rafts are small rafts or rubber boats kept on ships and boats for emergencies.
exercise: «The children built rafts from old barrels and planks.» What are rafts in this sentence? | Small, sharp stones on a path | *Flat platforms that float on water | Tall towers of stone | Heavy coats for winter
exercise: «There were rafts of leaves floating down the stream.» What does rafts of mean here? | Wooden boats with sails | Only three | Hidden under the water | *Lots of
exercise: «Sam rafts across the lake every weekend.» What does rafts mean here? | *Travels on a raft | Builds a tall tower | Swims very fast | Fishes with a net
test: In a design and technology lesson, groups test their model rafts. What are they checking? | *Which raft floats best and carries the most weight | How fast the wind blows | How many people can sing on it | Which raft is the most colourful
test: «Life rafts were stored on the ship in case of an emergency.» What is a life raft? | A rope for tying boats together | A large ship for holidays | A kind of fish | *A small raft or rubber boat for emergencies
exam: Which meaning of rafts fits «Rafts of people filled the beach»? | Lost and alone | *Lots of | To travel on a raft | A flat platform on water
